    "engine": "jupyter",
    "markdown": "---\ngd-head-tags:\n  - >-\n    `<script type=\"application/ld+json\">[{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"SoftwareSourceCode\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\", \"description\":\n    \"High-performance graph analysis library\", \"codeRepository\":\n    \"https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase\", \"license\":\n    \"https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT\", \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"documentation\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"programmingLanguage\": {\"@type\":\n    \"ComputerLanguage\", \"name\": \"Python\"}}, {\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"WebPage\", \"name\": \"Graph.all_triads - EdgeCase\", \"isPartOf\":\n    {\"@type\": \"WebSite\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\"}, \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase/reference/Graph.all_triads.html\"}]</script>`{=html}\nopen-graph:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.all_triads()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n    .doc-label-method} | EdgeCase\n  description: List every triad (set of three nodes) of a directed graph.\ntwitter-card:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.all_triads()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n    .doc-label-method} | EdgeCase\n  description: List every triad (set of three nodes) of a directed graph.\ntitle: >-\n  [Graph.all_triads()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n  .doc-label-method}\nbody-classes: doc-api-page doc-py-api-page\nshift-heading-level-by: 0\nbread-crumbs: false\ntoc-depth: 3\ndescription-meta: List every triad (set of three nodes) of a directed graph.\npage-navigation: false\nhtml-table-processing: none\n---\n\n::: {.doc-subject}\n\nList every triad (set of three nodes) of a directed graph.\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-usage-source}\nUsage\n\n[Source](https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase/blob/main/python/edgecase/graph.py#L40802-L40876){target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"}\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-signature .doc-function}\n```pythonsignature\nGraph.all_triads()\n```\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-text}\n\n![All triads](../assets/graphs/all-triads.light.svg){.lightbox fig-alt=\"Left: a directed graph with four nodes, ids 1 to 4, and no edges. Right: one miniature per triad, its three nodes in the accent color and the fourth faded, labeled with the id triple returned: (1, 2, 3), (1, 2, 4), (1, 3, 4), and (2, 3, 4), the 4 ways to choose 3 of 4 nodes.\" width=\"100%\"}\n\nReturns all $\\binom{n}{3}$ triples of nodes, each standing for the triad it induces.\nCombine with `triad_type()` to examine individual triads, or use `triads_by_type()` to\ngroup them.\n:::\n\n## Returns {.doc-returns}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code> [list[tuple[int, int, int]]]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   Every triple of node IDs, in ascending order. (NetworkX yields the induced subgraphs\n    instead.)\n:::\n\n## Raises {.doc-raises}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code> [ValueError]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   If the graph is undirected.\n:::\n\n## Technical Notes {.doc-technical-notes}\n\nCombinations of the node IDs, $O(n^3)$ triples.\n\n## See Also {.doc-see-also}\n\n[](`~triad_type`) \n\n:   Classify one triad.\n\n[](`~triads_by_type`) \n\n:   Group the triads by type.\n\n## Examples {.doc-examples}\n\nA directed graph on four nodes has four triads, one for each node left out:\n\n::: {#441d95f1 .cell execution_count=1}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nimport edgecase as ec\n\ngraph = ec.Graph.from_edges(\n    [(\"A\", \"B\"), (\"B\", \"C\"), (\"C\", \"D\")], directed=True\n)\n[[graph.get_label_from_id(n) for n in t] for t in graph.all_triads()]\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=1}\n```\n[['A', 'B', 'C'], ['A', 'B', 'D'], ['A', 'C', 'D'], ['B', 'C', 'D']]\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\n### The triads around one account\n\n`payments()` is a month of payments between 18 accounts at a made-up bank, each directed\nfrom payer to payee. Its 18 accounts form 816 triads. The 136 that include the Grocer\nshow its place in the network: it is paid by many accounts and pays no one, so 23 of\nthem are two accounts that both pay it (`021U`), and in none does the Grocer pay:\n\n::: {#dab5b1c6 .cell execution_count=2}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nfrom collections import Counter\n\npayments = ec.payments()\ngrocer = payments.get_id_from_label(\"Grocer\")\naround = [triad for triad in payments.all_triads() if grocer in triad]\n\nlen(payments.all_triads()), Counter(\n    payments.triad_type(list(triad)) for triad in around\n)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=2}\n```\n(816,\n Counter({'012': 60,\n          '003': 32,\n          '021U': 23,\n          '021D': 8,\n          '021C': 8,\n          '030T': 3,\n          '120U': 2}))\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\n::: {#142659a1 .cell execution_count=3}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\npayments.plot(\n    highlight=[(payer, \"Grocer\") for payer in\n               [\"Dee\", \"Eve\", \"Max\", \"Nia\", \"Hal\", \"Lena\", \"Ana\", \"Gus\"]],\n    label_by=\"label\", seed=11, height=420,\n)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=3}\n```{=html}\n<div class=\"ec-theme\" style=\"display:contents\"><style class=\"ec-theme-vars\">:where(.ec-theme){--ect-3239c383:#fafafa;--ect-e5dfd507:#94a3b8;--ect-8a2de1d4:#374151;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(15,23,42,0.88);--ect-21ade003:#f1f5f9;--ect-61169ea5:#c2410c;--ect-63cc1385:#d4d4d8;--ect-879b7ebc:#949497;--ect-b9f8de6d:#872d08;--ect-f59ba8df:#a1a1aa}@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark){.ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#0d1117;--ect-e5dfd507:#4b5563;--ect-8a2de1d4:#d1d5db;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(241,245,249,0.92);--ect-21ade003:#0f172a;--ect-61169ea5:#f97316;--ect-63cc1385:#3f3f46;--ect-879b7ebc:#2c2c31;--ect-b9f8de6d:#ae500f;--ect-f59ba8df:#71717a}}:is(html.quarto-light, body.quarto-light, html[data-bs-theme=\"light\"], [data-jp-theme-light=\"true\"], body.vscode-light, body.vscode-high-contrast-light, html[theme=\"light\"]) .ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#fafafa;--ect-e5dfd507:#94a3b8;--ect-8a2de1d4:#374151;--ect-57425a7e: